{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>YHWH</b> — [concerning] דוי, it is a noun, like מדוה." "<b>He sustains him</b> — little by little as the illness turns, or [it means] the turning of his words and affairs upon his bed. And the correct interpretation: that you have turned [him] to face HaShem, and the meaning is figurative, that you turn him upon his bed from side to side and sustain him. And the meaning: for there is no need for the children of men to sustain him."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:30:28.640010146Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}